{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`_reads._tracker` raises `store_uninitialized` only when the tracker directory is ABSENT\n(`src/rebar/_reads.py`, `if not os.path.isdir(tracker)`). A directory that EXISTS but is not a\nusable store — no `.git`, or a `.git` with no resolvable HEAD, or one mid-clone — satisfies\n`isdir`, so every read returns `[]`. The caller cannot distinguish \"this store is empty\" from\n\"this store is broken\", which is the exact confusion the guard was added to remove.\n\n## Encountered three times, each independently\n\n1. **In production.** The deployed MCP server served an EMPTY tracker for an extended period —\n   the store dir held `reviewbot-ensure-tickets` marker files and no `.git`; `isdir` was true so\n   the guard never fired and `rebar.list_tickets()` returned `READ_OK count=0`. Proven on the box.\n2. **`fathomable-yester-thrip` (change 2244, merged).** `clear_tracker_dir` empties CONTENTS but\n   leaves the directory, so between clear and a completed clone reads return `[]`. Recorded there\n   as a residual, not fixed.\n3. **`unfit-beneficial-whimbrel` AC3.** \"While the clone is in flight, tracker reads report\n   `store_uninitialized` rather than `[]`\" — NOT met, same reason; left unticked, points here.\n\n## Why the obvious fixes do not apply\n\nThe MCP deployment's tracker path is itself a MOUNT POINT (`/dev/nvme1n1`, xfs, per `/proc/mounts`),\nso the directory cannot be removed and nothing renamed over it — the entrypoint clears contents,\nnot the directory. The fix has to be on the READ side.\n\n## Constraint the fix must respect\n\nAn EXISTING but empty INITIALIZED store must still read `[]` — that is a real contract with an\nexisting test (`tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py`: \"An EXISTING but empty store is\nNOT an error\"). So the discriminator cannot be emptiness. It has to be \"is this a usable\nstore\": a resolvable git HEAD. `.env-id` is ruled out as the read predicate (git-ignored,\nabsent right after a valid clone; cf. `ab61-f3e8-6ee6-4905`).\n\n## Blast radius\n\n`_reads._tracker` funnels 7 read entry points, so this changes core read semantics repo-wide —\nthe reason it was scoped out of 2244.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A tracker directory that exists but is NOT a usable store reads as `store_uninitialized`,\n      not `[]`.\n- [ ] An existing, empty, INITIALIZED store still reads `[]` — the existing contract test\n      continues to pass unmodified.\n- [ ] A store mid-clone (directory present, HEAD not yet resolvable) reads as uninitialized.\n- [ ] Regression coverage fails if the predicate reverts to a bare `os.path.isdir`.\n\n---\n\n## Fix plan (operator-APPROVED; rebar-debug Phase 2)\n\n**Root cause (proven; full RCA in prior comment).** `_reads._tracker()` gates the read path\non `os.path.isdir(tracker)` only; a dir that exists but has no `.git`, or `.git` with an\nunresolvable HEAD, satisfies `isdir`, so the guard never fires and reads yield `[]`.\nAttributed to `44fd-230c-5893-4246` (commit `84fc5f9b`).\n\n**Approved change.** Broaden the read-side init predicate so a present-but-unusable store raises\n`store_uninitialized` instead of `[]`, across all library/MCP read entry points (the ~7 funneling\nthrough `_reads._tracker`; MCP read tools delegate to these facades). Predicate: `.git` present\nAND `git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` resolves. The masking removed is the one that misleads a\nDRIVING AGENT on the read path (library/CLI/MCP); the audit web index is a deliberately different\nread-only consumer (see caller gate).\n\n**Gate model (three gates; NOT identical -- see comment).** `event_prepare._ensure_initialized`\n(`.git`), `_seam.append_event` (`.env-id`, authoritative write gate), and `_reads._tracker`.\nReads deliberately do NOT adopt `.env-id` (git-ignored local state absent right after a valid\nclone, which must stay readable). This closes the `.git`/HEAD read/write disagreement only.\n\n**Design.** New stdlib-only leaf `src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py::store_is_usable(tracker)`\n= isdir AND `.git` present AND HEAD resolves (git via `git -C tracker`; `.git`-exists check\nprecedes the HEAD probe so git cannot walk up to the parent code repo). `subprocess.run` uses\n`check=False`: a clean non-zero rc == \"HEAD unresolvable\" -> not usable; an OSError (git binary\nmissing) is a DISTINCT environment failure that PROPAGATES rather than collapsing into\n`store_uninitialized` (advisory T5b; test-pinned). Both `_reads._tracker` and\n`event_prepare._ensure_initialized` call it -- the write gate thereby also rejects a mid-clone\nstore, proven safe for init (see comment). The leaf keeps `_reads` out of the write-core import SCC.\n\n**Files.**\n- `src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py` (new) -- shared `store_is_usable`.\n- `src/rebar/_reads.py` -- `_tracker` raises `store_uninitialized` when `not store_is_usable`.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py` -- `_ensure_initialized` calls the shared predicate.\n- `src/rebar/audit/server.py` -- reconcile the one consumer (docstring + log; behavior unchanged).\n- `tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py` -- read + write-gate + predicate + audit regression.\n\n**Caller-dependency gate + reconciliation (addresses plan-review BLOCK G6).** The only consumer\nof `store_uninitialized` is `rebar.audit.server._audited_tickets`, a read-only WEB index whose\ncorrect failure mode is \"render an empty page, not 500\". Under the OLD read semantics a\npresent-but-unusable store read `[]`, so it ALSO rendered empty there -- behavior is unchanged by\nthis fix. BUT that module's docstring promised \"a genuinely broken store is not silently blanked\",\na promise that held only because broken stores did not raise `store_uninitialized`. This fix makes\nthem raise it, so the promise is now false. Reconcile HONESTLY (no behavior change): the index\nstill degrades any `store_uninitialized` (absent OR present-but-unusable) to empty because a\nread-only web index must not 500; correct the docstring to state that; and broaden the WARNING log\nso a present-but-unusable store is LOGGED (not silently blanked) -- operators diagnose store health\nvia the driving agent/CLI, which now surfaces the distinction. No caller depends on the old\n`[]`-for-broken-store on the driving-agent path.\n\n**Acceptance criteria (each evidenced by a test in the named file).**\n- [ ] READ: tracker dir exists but no `.git` -> raises `store_uninitialized`, not `[]`\n      (drive `rebar.list_tickets`; assert `error_code_for(exc) == \"store_uninitialized\"`).\n- [ ] READ: mid-clone (`.git` present, HEAD unresolvable) -> raises `store_uninitialized`.\n- [ ] READ: existing empty INITIALIZED store still reads `[]` (existing contract test unchanged).\n- [ ] READ: valid clone with resolvable HEAD but NO `.env-id` still reads successfully\n      (asserts reads/writes deliberately differ on `.env-id`).\n- [ ] WRITE: `event_prepare._ensure_initialized` rejects a mid-clone store and still accepts an\n      initialized store (covers the write-gate behavior change).\n- [ ] PREDICATE: `store_is_usable` is False for absent/no-`.git`/mid-clone, True for an\n      initialized store and a HEAD-resolvable clone without `.env-id`.\n- [ ] PREDICATE: a missing `git` binary (OSError) PROPAGATES from `store_is_usable` rather than\n      being reported as `store_uninitialized` (T5b failure-taxonomy).\n- [ ] AUDIT: `audit.server._audited_tickets` renders empty (returns `[]`) AND logs a warning for a\n      present-but-unusable store, and still propagates a non-`store_uninitialized` failure.\n- [ ] Regression: reverting the predicate to bare `os.path.isdir` returns broken/mid-clone to RED\n      (defect-seeded mutation check).\n\n**Verification.** RED->GREEN in the named test file: broken/mid-clone READ and write-gate\nmid-clone cases RED pre-fix, GREEN post-fix; empty-init and no-`.env-id`-clone stay `[]`; mutation\nto bare `isdir` returns to RED. Read + write suites stay green.\n\n**Out of approved scope (parity -- discovered tickets):** CLI read path (`reads_cli.py`) and\nother bare-`isdir` read sites -- Step 7 parity sweep."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787959475386155001,"uuid":"aa73a5bf-f92c-4aed-8d9c-c83a5986a206"}